From: Kestrel local diagnostic build
Subject: [PATCH 0019] arm64: dts: Slim3: close I2C9 keyboard dependencies

Restore the configured keyboard fixed rail and GPI1 supplier without
re-enabling reset-associated GEM NoC. Delete only I2C9 ICC properties to
use the already-tested diagnostic no-vote mechanism. Existing hardware
voltages, IRQ, GPIO, DMA mask and IOMMU mapping remain unchanged.
Applies after diagnostic series 0018 (dt21/dt23 hardware baseline).
Local-only bring-up patch, not upstream-ready or production bus voting.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x126100-lenovo-ideapad-slim3.dts
@@ -1811,3 +1811,21 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* DIAGNOSTIC (0019): restore only the configured I2C9 keyboard supply
+ * and its existing GPI1 DMA provider. GEM remains disabled after native
+ * resets; use the same narrowly scoped NULL/no-vote ICC path as I2C5.
+ * Keep voltage, GPIO, IRQ, DMA channel/mask and IOMMU definitions intact.
+ * No display, PCIe, NVMe or other controller enablement. Local-only.
+ */
+&vreg_misc_3p3 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&i2c9 {
+	/delete-property/ interconnects;
+	/delete-property/ interconnect-names;
+};
+
+&gpi_dma1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
